to someone, at least try and learn to be

00:09:56.959 --> 00:10:02.480
more direct. Somebody once told me that

00:09:59.839 --> 00:10:04.000
being kind is also about being direct.

00:10:02.480 --> 00:10:06.000
That's actually my life coach, and every

00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:07.680
life coach also needs a life coach. So,

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:09.200
if you don't really know how to say

00:10:07.680 --> 00:10:11.279
something and you're afraid of how it's

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:12.880
going to come across and you're already

00:10:11.279 --> 00:10:14.560
judging yourself for what other people

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:15.839
would judge you on before the words even

00:10:14.560 --> 00:10:17.200
come out of your mouth and you're just

00:10:15.839 --> 00:10:18.480
being wishywashy and not getting to the

00:10:17.200 --> 00:10:20.160
point and being passive aggressive, then

00:10:18.480 --> 00:10:22.000
you're only wasting everybody's time and

00:10:20.160 --> 00:10:24.720
energy too. So, if you really care about

00:10:22.000 --> 00:10:27.600
yourself and other people, be direct.

00:10:24.720 --> 00:10:29.200
The next one is O own the anger. And

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:31.279
this is the part nobody wants but

00:10:29.200 --> 00:10:33.920
everybody needs. Okay? Under every

00:10:31.279 --> 00:10:36.640
single people pleasing pattern, there is

00:10:33.920 --> 00:10:39.040
anger. It's just been buried so deeply

00:10:36.640 --> 00:10:41.040
because anger is that one emotion that

00:10:39.040 --> 00:10:42.640
you are absolutely maybe not even

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:45.040
allowed to have. You're not allowed to

00:10:42.640 --> 00:10:47.040
be angry about your situation because

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:48.560
you should be more grateful that you

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:49.760
have, you know, a roof over your head,

00:10:48.560 --> 00:10:51.600
for example, and you have food and

00:10:49.760 --> 00:10:53.360
water, which you should be, but it

00:10:51.600 --> 00:10:55.920
doesn't come at the cost of being

00:10:53.360 --> 00:10:58.000
abused. Okay? For example, an anger may

00:10:55.920 --> 00:11:00.399
have gotten you punished. Anger got you

00:10:58.000 --> 00:11:03.360
called difficult, dramatic, or maybe you

00:11:00.399 --> 00:11:06.480
were too much. So early on you learned

00:11:03.360 --> 00:11:10.800
to convert that anger into other things.

00:11:06.480 --> 00:11:13.200
Anxiety, guilt, shame into physical

00:11:10.800 --> 00:11:15.680
symptoms, maybe a stomach ache into

00:11:13.200 --> 00:11:18.640
being too nice to everyone, even to

00:11:15.680 --> 00:11:21.360
people who don't deserve that at all,

00:11:18.640 --> 00:11:23.040
and you're still so nice to them. So I

00:11:21.360 --> 00:11:26.240
want you to hear this very clearly,

00:11:23.040 --> 00:11:27.680
okay? Anger is protective. It's not a

00:11:26.240 --> 00:11:29.920
character flaw. It's your nervous

00:11:27.680 --> 00:11:32.880
system's way of telling you that a

00:11:29.920 --> 00:11:34.800
boundary or a line just got crossed and

00:11:32.880 --> 00:11:36.160
you deserve better than that. So, I know

00:11:34.800 --> 00:11:37.680
that a lot of the spiritual space

00:11:36.160 --> 00:11:40.000
especially is going to tell you to

00:11:37.680 --> 00:11:41.760
transcend that anger, to bypass it, and

00:11:40.000 --> 00:11:43.279
raise your vibration above it because

00:11:41.760 --> 00:11:45.040
it's a negative energy and you don't

00:11:43.279 --> 00:11:47.040
want to spend time, you know, being in

00:11:45.040 --> 00:11:49.040
these low vibrational modes. And I'm not

00:11:47.040 --> 00:11:51.040
going to tell you that because that's a

00:11:49.040 --> 00:11:53.920
lie that continues to keep people small.

00:11:51.040 --> 00:11:56.399
You can't just bypass any emotions that

00:11:53.920 --> 00:11:58.000
that you never actually have processed

00:11:56.399 --> 00:11:59.440
yourself. All you can do is to continue

00:11:58.000 --> 00:12:01.440
to press it down and you call it

00:11:59.440 --> 00:12:03.279
enlightenment, but you're absolutely

00:12:01.440 --> 00:12:05.360
allowed to be angry. You're allowed to

00:12:03.279 --> 00:12:07.600
be angry that you had to be the one

00:12:05.360 --> 00:12:09.120
that's easier than other people and you

00:12:07.600 --> 00:12:10.720
had to meet other people's needs, but

00:12:09.120 --> 00:12:12.720
nobody cared about your needs. And

00:12:10.720 --> 00:12:15.279
you're allowed to be angry that you're

00:12:12.720 --> 00:12:17.360
the child that's managing the adults in

00:12:15.279 --> 00:12:19.279
your life and you had to be the adult.

00:12:17.360 --> 00:12:20.800
And feeling that anger, by the way, is

00:12:19.279 --> 00:12:22.399
not going to make you a bitter person

00:12:20.800 --> 00:12:24.800
because people who actually swallow

00:12:22.399 --> 00:12:26.720
their anger are the ones who become

00:12:24.800 --> 00:12:28.240
bitter about everything and they become

00:12:26.720 --> 00:12:30.079
victims, okay? And they project that

00:12:28.240 --> 00:12:32.880
onto everyone else in their life. You

00:12:30.079 --> 00:12:35.120
have to channel it out. That anger is

00:12:32.880 --> 00:12:36.800
the exact thing that will get you off

00:12:35.120 --> 00:12:39.519
the floor because on the other side of

00:12:36.800 --> 00:12:41.279
it is the sentence that you've unable to

00:12:39.519 --> 00:12:44.399
say out loud that everything that you've

00:12:41.279 --> 00:12:46.880
gone through is not okay and that you

00:12:44.399 --> 00:12:49.200
deserve better. So try and think about

00:12:46.880 --> 00:12:51.680
something that you're really angry about

00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:55.279
right now and just finish that sentence

00:12:51.680 --> 00:12:56.959
off with and I deserve better than that.

00:12:55.279 --> 00:12:58.480
If it helps you, maybe even journal it

00:12:56.959 --> 00:13:00.399
out or write it down, but you don't have

00:12:58.480 --> 00:13:02.160
to send this to anybody or post it and

00:13:00.399 --> 00:13:04.240
you're writing this for yourself. You're

00:13:02.160 --> 00:13:06.079
confirming it for your own body and your

00:13:04.240 --> 00:13:07.839
own mind. Or you can go outside and you

00:13:06.079 --> 00:13:09.839
can channel it out. Do something

00:13:07.839 --> 00:13:11.519
physical with your body. Go for a walk

00:13:09.839 --> 00:13:13.920
and walk really fast. Go lift something

00:13:11.519 --> 00:13:17.120
heavy. Go hiking. Go swimming. Whatever

00:13:13.920 --> 00:13:19.760
it is, anger is a very mobilizing

00:13:17.120 --> 00:13:21.920
emotion. It really gets you going, which

00:13:19.760 --> 00:13:23.920
means your anger wants to go somewhere.

00:13:21.920 --> 00:13:25.680
So, give it someplace to go. And baby,

00:13:23.920 --> 00:13:29.040
don't unleash it in my comment section,

00:13:25.680 --> 00:13:31.120
please. The next is O. Offer yourself

00:13:29.040 --> 00:13:33.200
evidence. I think a lot of us are not

00:13:31.120 --> 00:13:35.920
able to believe ourselves when we say

00:13:33.200 --> 00:13:37.519
things like, you know, I am confident. I

00:13:35.920 --> 00:13:39.440
have a lot of self-esteem. And this is

00:13:37.519 --> 00:13:41.360
also why the idea of affirmations can

00:13:39.440 --> 00:13:43.040
fail for a lot of people. You may stand

00:13:41.360 --> 00:13:45.040
in front of a mirror and say stuff like,

00:13:43.040 --> 00:13:47.200
you know, I'm confident. And your brain,

00:13:45.040 --> 00:13:49.120
which is not stupid, by the way. It's

00:13:47.200 --> 00:13:51.920
very intelligent, will go, okay, but

00:13:49.120 --> 00:13:53.680
based on what exactly? Your brain runs

00:13:51.920 --> 00:13:55.279
on evidence. So, if you want to change

00:13:53.680 --> 00:13:56.880
what you believe about yourself, you

00:13:55.279 --> 00:13:59.279
don't have to repeat something and hope

00:13:56.880 --> 00:14:01.519
that it sticks around. You have to give

00:13:59.279 --> 00:14:02.959
it proof over time. You have to do it.

00:14:01.519 --> 00:14:04.959
I'm not a therapist and this is not

00:14:02.959 --> 00:14:06.880
therapy, but this is one technique that

00:14:04.959 --> 00:14:08.560
anyone may find helpful and that my

00:14:06.880 --> 00:14:10.880
therapist also taught me. You can take a

00:14:08.560 --> 00:14:13.600
small box, maybe a jar or a tin,

00:14:10.880 --> 00:14:15.920
whatever it is. Every day you write one

00:14:13.600 --> 00:14:17.839
thing down. On a stick of paper, you can

00:14:15.920 --> 00:14:19.279
use both sides. Maybe on one side you

00:14:17.839 --> 00:14:21.279
write your affirmation and on the other

00:14:19.279 --> 00:14:23.360
side you write the evidence. So on the

00:14:21.279 --> 00:14:25.120
front you can say I am someone who

00:14:23.360 --> 00:14:27.440
follows through and on the back you can

00:14:25.120 --> 00:14:29.199
say I said I will call my friend back on

00:14:27.440 --> 00:14:31.360
Sunday and I did. Something like that.

00:14:29.199 --> 00:14:32.800
So whenever you need confirmation that

00:14:31.360 --> 00:14:34.240
you can do things, you can put an

00:14:32.800 --> 00:14:35.680
affirmation out and you read it.

00:14:34.240 --> 00:14:37.760
Basically, you're learning how to become

00:14:35.680 --> 00:14:39.440
the source of your own evidence and

00:14:37.760 --> 00:14:41.279
you're cutting out the middleman. You're

00:14:39.440 --> 00:14:43.360
basically no longer waiting for a second

00:14:41.279 --> 00:14:45.199
person to notice that you're kind,

00:14:43.360 --> 00:14:47.360
you're capable, or you're funny because

00:14:45.199 --> 00:14:49.600
now you have this box with the receipts

00:14:47.360 --> 00:14:51.680
inside and you wrote them yourself and

00:14:49.600 --> 00:14:53.279
they're all true. Maybe at first you

00:14:51.680 --> 00:14:54.880
might feel a bit embarrassing like why

00:14:53.279 --> 00:14:56.480
am I doing this, right? The first week

00:14:54.880 --> 00:14:58.320
you might feel a bit silly like, oh,

00:14:56.480 --> 00:15:00.079
writing things down like I am a good

00:14:58.320 --> 00:15:02.160
friend on a piece of paper, but do it

00:15:00.079 --> 00:15:04.240
anyway. Trust me, I did this like last

00:15:02.160 --> 00:15:06.240
year for example. I was so scared to

00:15:04.240 --> 00:15:08.480
jump out of a boat and people on my

00:15:06.240 --> 00:15:09.920
group trip like they had to sort of like

00:15:08.480 --> 00:15:11.279
encourage me like, "Come on, you taught

00:15:09.920 --> 00:15:12.240
us so much. Like you have to do this

00:15:11.279 --> 00:15:13.839
yourself." And I'm like, "You're so

00:15:12.240 --> 00:15:15.600
right. I have to do this." And I had to

00:15:13.839 --> 00:15:17.839
prove to myself that I can absolutely

00:15:15.600 --> 00:15:19.440
like jump out of a boat and I won't be,

00:15:17.839 --> 00:15:21.440
you know, injured and I'll be completely

00:15:19.440 --> 00:15:23.440
fine. And I was fine. So this year,

00:15:21.440 --> 00:15:25.279
especially for, you know, my friends who

00:15:23.440 --> 00:15:27.839
came back on my group trip, they got to

00:15:25.279 --> 00:15:29.680
witness me jump out of boats and do more

00:15:27.839 --> 00:15:31.360
exciting things and be more daring with

00:15:29.680 --> 00:15:32.639
myself and my physical body. Because

00:15:31.360 --> 00:15:35.120
over the last year, I've been able to

00:15:32.639 --> 00:15:37.279
practice jumping and diving and do all

00:15:35.120 --> 00:15:39.120
these things. And I've been able to

00:15:37.279 --> 00:15:41.360
prove all of these things to myself

00:15:39.120 --> 00:15:44.000
because look, recovery can feel low-key

00:15:41.360 --> 00:15:46.160
embarrassing at first before it becomes

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:48.079
so beautiful and you just witness all of

00:15:46.160 --> 00:15:50.320
the fruits of your labor and that's

00:15:48.079 --> 00:15:52.800
amazing. And also like guess what? This

00:15:50.320 --> 00:15:55.279
is also why we heal in silence because

00:15:52.800 --> 00:15:56.959
nobody else has to see this but you and

00:15:55.279 --> 00:15:59.680
you do this only for yourself and not

00:15:56.959 --> 00:16:01.839
for other people. This is only for you.

00:15:59.680 --> 00:16:03.600
So don't feel ashamed about anything

00:16:01.839 --> 00:16:06.000
because literally nobody's going to see

00:16:03.600 --> 00:16:09.759
it. T

00:16:06.000 --> 00:16:12.240
unpopular action. So new insight does

00:16:09.759 --> 00:16:15.279
not change existing behavior. New

00:16:12.240 --> 00:16:17.600
behavior changes existing behavior. You

00:16:15.279 --> 00:16:20.240
have to start doing things that other

00:16:17.600 --> 00:16:22.399
people might not like from you on

00:16:20.240 --> 00:16:24.639
purpose. Small things like not like a

00:16:22.399 --> 00:16:26.399
dramatic big fight or confrontation.

00:16:24.639 --> 00:16:28.639
Like we're not cutting anyone off just

00:16:26.399 --> 00:16:31.120
yet, but I'm talking about the small

00:16:28.639 --> 00:16:32.560
micro doses. Tell people that the

00:16:31.120 --> 00:16:35.360
restaurant that you actually want to go

00:16:32.560 --> 00:16:36.480
to is that way. Or say things like, "Oh,

00:16:35.360 --> 00:16:38.000
you know what? Actually, I don't want to

00:16:36.480 --> 00:16:39.839
do that to something that's very low

00:16:38.000 --> 00:16:41.440
stakes. I'm going to go home early and

00:16:39.839 --> 00:16:43.680
rest and I'm feeling kind of tired

00:16:41.440 --> 00:16:46.160
today, so I'm going to do something for

00:16:43.680 --> 00:16:48.639
myself." Or if you have a risky text

00:16:46.160 --> 00:16:50.399
that you need to send, send it, but

00:16:48.639 --> 00:16:52.079
don't soften it, right? And then, you

00:16:50.399 --> 00:16:53.600
know, put your phone down and don't look

00:16:52.079 --> 00:16:55.440
at your phone for the next 3 hours. And

00:16:53.600 --> 00:16:57.279
while you're doing that, try not to use

00:16:55.440 --> 00:17:00.639
minimizing words that take your power

00:16:57.279 --> 00:17:03.199
away. Words like just or sorry, just a

00:17:00.639 --> 00:17:04.400
second. Say, "One second, please." Or if

00:17:03.199 --> 00:17:07.280
you bump into someone, you can say,

00:17:04.400 --> 00:17:09.039
"Pardon me or excuse me, not sorry."

00:17:07.280 --> 00:17:11.679
Because that's not your fault. Okay?

00:17:09.039 --> 00:17:13.600
Like I have a rule why I only say sorry

00:17:11.679 --> 00:17:15.679
if it's my fault. Then here's also the

00:17:13.600 --> 00:17:17.520
somatic part of it aside from words

00:17:15.679 --> 00:17:19.039
because words really are spells and they

00:17:17.520 --> 00:17:20.240
really control you and control your

00:17:19.039 --> 00:17:22.720
life. And you know I'm trying to get

00:17:20.240 --> 00:17:25.120
better at my own words too because when

00:17:22.720 --> 00:17:27.120
you first do it you might even feel a

00:17:25.120 --> 00:17:29.360
sensation not just in your head but in

00:17:27.120 --> 00:17:31.440
your body. You might feel some heat

00:17:29.360 --> 00:17:33.600
building in your chest, maybe a drop in

00:17:31.440 --> 00:17:34.880
your stomach and maybe even a joke of

00:17:33.600 --> 00:17:37.360
like, "Oh my god, what if they got so

00:17:34.880 --> 00:17:40.000
upset with me?" Your body may read this

00:17:37.360 --> 00:17:42.160
as danger because for a long time it

00:17:40.000 --> 00:17:44.559
might be dangerous to you. So don't fix

00:17:42.160 --> 00:17:46.559
it by double texting or apologizing for

00:17:44.559 --> 00:17:49.039
something that you didn't do wrong. Just

00:17:46.559 --> 00:17:51.280
breathe and just stay and just let your

00:17:49.039 --> 00:17:53.520
body find out that like look nothing bad

00:17:51.280 --> 00:17:55.200
happened and that is it. I love this one

00:17:53.520 --> 00:17:56.880
thing actually in the Mediterranean

00:17:55.200 --> 00:17:59.760
instead of saying like oh I'm so sorry

00:17:56.880 --> 00:18:01.440
if you bump into someone you say oa like

00:17:59.760 --> 00:18:02.880
oops you know happy accident. I love

00:18:01.440 --> 00:18:05.120
that. And that's sort of another way

00:18:02.880 --> 00:18:07.840
that our bodies and our nervous systems

00:18:05.120 --> 00:18:10.240
can learn how to feel safer through

00:18:07.840 --> 00:18:12.080
repeated evidence and not through, you

00:18:10.240 --> 00:18:13.679
know, understanding or through theory.

00:18:12.080 --> 00:18:16.000
We really have to practice these things

00:18:13.679 --> 00:18:18.080
and let it be uncomfortable and survive

00:18:16.000 --> 00:18:20.160
that and then do it again and again

00:18:18.080 --> 00:18:21.840
until your body can, you know, finally

00:18:20.160 --> 00:18:23.440
update your mind like, you know what,

00:18:21.840 --> 00:18:25.679
I've done this five times, 10 times

00:18:23.440 --> 00:18:27.679
already. This is going to be fine. So,

00:18:25.679 --> 00:18:29.440
and this is also why like I get so

00:18:27.679 --> 00:18:30.960
emotional like watching my people do

00:18:29.440 --> 00:18:32.480
this in real time during my group trip

00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:34.160
in Greece because I really get to see

00:18:32.480 --> 00:18:35.600
it. So, for example, on the trip that we

00:18:34.160 --> 00:18:37.440
went to in Greece, we would have a whole

00:18:35.600 --> 00:18:38.720
day planned like gorgeous everything.

00:18:37.440 --> 00:18:40.320
And then someone would come to me and

00:18:38.720 --> 00:18:42.160
say, "Honestly, I feel really tired. I

00:18:40.320 --> 00:18:43.840
think I need to stay back and rest." And

00:18:42.160 --> 00:18:45.520
I would say, "Amazing. Do what's best

00:18:43.840 --> 00:18:47.360
for you." Because here's what I know.

00:18:45.520 --> 00:18:49.039
There will always be another boat trip.

00:18:47.360 --> 00:18:50.799
There will always be another island,

00:18:49.039 --> 00:18:53.440
another sunset, another group trip

00:18:50.799 --> 00:18:56.240
together. And what there won't always be

00:18:53.440 --> 00:18:58.320
though is you choosing yourself and your

00:18:56.240 --> 00:19:00.640
health in a moment where it would have

00:18:58.320 --> 00:19:03.039
been easier to just go along and go with

00:19:00.640 --> 00:19:04.799
everyone else even though you don't feel

00:19:03.039 --> 00:19:06.080
like it. And that's honestly one of the

00:19:04.799 --> 00:19:07.760
most beautiful things that I get to

00:19:06.080 --> 00:19:09.840
witness and I still do keep in touch

00:19:07.760 --> 00:19:11.120
with everyone who goes on my group trips

00:19:09.840 --> 00:19:12.559
if they want to keep in touch with me

00:19:11.120 --> 00:19:14.559
that is. But I get to watch these

00:19:12.559 --> 00:19:16.080
efforts compound like in real life

00:19:14.559 --> 00:19:18.080
because now I get to see them and they

00:19:16.080 --> 00:19:20.000
see me. So that's really amazing to me

00:19:18.080 --> 00:19:22.320
is the ability to witness all that

00:19:20.000 --> 00:19:23.760
growth. oxygen mask. So, if you feel

